**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Copying experiments brings the items they use, each mapped onto a kit item or added (001 §H; .spec-md §3.15; the S7.2 brief; the S6 mapper's request: `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` gains the item mapping, its read-then-write order and its report kept). Each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs`: `KitLibraryError` (step 139) gains `KitLibraryItemErr of ItemError`, an item the copy could not take, rendered `the items could not be copied: <e.describe>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`: `ExperimentCopyReport` (step 224) gains `items : Item list` after `experiments`, each item added to the kit as written. `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` (step 224) takes `(itemRows : ItemCopyRow list)` after `ids`, the user's choices; an item no row names takes its default (step 221). After reading the kept experiments (224 (b)) it reads `source.proxy.readItems ()` and `this.proxy.readItems ()` (step 218); the used items MUST be the Ok result of `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` of the kept experiments and the source's items, with its typed error returned as KitLibraryItemErr before any write; the rows `ItemCopyRow.copyRowsFor used <the kit's items> itemRows`, and the items to add `ItemCopyRow.itemsToAdd rows <the kit's items>` (step 221), a refusal answering `KitLibraryItemErr` before anything is written. The closure (224 (c)) MUST walk source-owned unassigned descriptor bindings followed by the added items' libraryReferences (step 215), so every added item's exact model and physics snapshots come with it. References rewritten onto held target items MUST resolve through the target kit's snapshots before writing, not through the source library. The lab files read (224 (d)) are the kept experiments' `dataFileOpt` paths followed by the added items' `photoOpt` paths, each distinct path read once in order of first appearance. The writes (224 (f)) are the snapshots, then every lab file under step 224's folder and suffix rule, then each added item through `this.proxy.writeItem` (step 218), its `photoOpt` replaced by the attachment path of its copied photo, then the experiments, so a written item or experiment never references a file the kit lacks. For every descriptor with Some sourceId, the copied experiment MUST store Some targetId from its effective mapping row; AddCopiedItem MUST retain the added item's id. Descriptors with None MUST remain unassigned. Each mapped descriptor's library binding MUST be derived from the chosen target item's typed physics binding (preset id or sample version), and MUST be unbound for a standalone model rather than retain the source's unrelated binding. Placement, elementId and the varied element MUST be preserved. Before writes, the mapped experiments MUST resolve through Experiment.itemsUsedBy against held plus added target items, and each chosen target's exact model/binding snapshot closure MUST be resolved from the target kit; source closures MUST be read only for added items and source-owned unassigned descriptor bindings. Missing target dependencies MUST refuse the copy before writes, never silently import the source's model in their place. A mapped item file MUST remain byte-for-byte untouched, but its experiment binding MUST be rewritten. `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` MUST likewise resolve explicit ids through readItems before recording and snapshot their exact item/model closure as well as unassigned library bindings, returning KitLibraryItemErr for a missing id before writing. The same public resolver MUST be used after reopen by the copy panel, so the selected identity is consumed rather than merely suppressing an item file. No item relation MAY be reconstructed from shared presets. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the `CopyChosenExperiments` arm (step 225) passes `[]`, so a window's copy maps and adds each used item by its default until step 228 passes the panel's choices; on `Ok` it reads `model.kit.proxy.readItems ()` with the experiments and sets `kitItems` through step 223's content function. Tests, in `ExperimentCopyTests` (step 224), whose every existing fact passes `[]` and keeps its assertions. The source also holds items recorded through `recordItem` (step 219): `Laser600` (`SourcePresetChoice` of `PresetIds.source600`, used by E1), `ML` (`StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` at version 1, used by E1), `QZ` (`SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1, used by E2) and `CPL1` (the circular-polarizer item model, used by none). `a copy adds the items its experiments use, with their model snapshots`: copying [E1] with no row into an empty target answers a report whose `items` are Laser600 and ML; the target's `readItems` answers them, its `paths` hold `Laser600.item-json` and `ML.item-json` and every snapshot E1's closure needs, and neither QZ nor CPL1 is written. `an item the kit holds by id, or by model and label, is mapped and not added`: over a target holding ML (written through `writeItem`, the same id) and a `Laser600` of the same preset under another id, copying [E1] reports no item and leaves the target's item files unchanged. `an added item whose label the kit holds takes the next free label`: over a target holding an item labelled `ML` of the glass plate, copying [E1] adds the source's ML as `ML (2)`. `the user's choice overrides the default, and a choice the kit cannot take writes nothing`: over the target of the second fact, a row adding Laser600 adds it as `Laser600 (2)` while ML stays mapped; a row mapping ML onto a test-local GUID answers `KitLibraryItemErr (UnknownKitItemErr _)`, and a row adding ML, whose id the target holds, `KitLibraryItemErr (DuplicateItemIdErr _)`, each leaving the target's `paths` unchanged. `an added item's photo is copied with it`: with the source's ML given the photo `data/photos/ml.jpg` (attached through `attachLabFile`), copying [E1] writes `data/photos/ml.jpg` into the empty target and the added ML references it; over a target already holding another `data/photos/ml.jpg`, the copy is `data/photos/ml (2).jpg` and ML references that. `KitLibraryTests`' `every kit library error renders its condition and its payload` (step 139) covers `KitLibraryItemErr`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. Physical fixture bindings MUST be explicit: E1's source and sample descriptors name Laser600.id and ML.id; E2 names QZ.id. The other same-model pieces MUST remain unreferenced. `a copied experiment reopens using the explicitly selected target physical piece` MUST create two source pieces A and B of one preset/model with distinct ids and parameter values, bind only B, and select target T of that model with a third id and different parameters. With valid complete model snapshots on both sides, copy and reopen the target, resolve the copied experiment through Experiment.itemsUsedBy, and assert exactly T.id and T.parameters, excluding A and B; assert T's file is unchanged and no source-piece file was added. Repeat the positive branch with a standalone ItemModelVersionInstance to prove S6 does not wait for S8.2. `copying two same-model pieces preserves separate choices and shared use` MUST bind A and B in one experiment and B again in another, map A to target T and add B; reopen and assert the first experiment resolves T and B, the second resolves B once, with the correct model snapshots and B's photo. The missing-target-id and duplicate-add tests MUST start with fully valid bindings, model snapshots and data files, then alter only the choice; assert the exact ItemError and a byte-for-byte unchanged target tree, not an unrelated earlier failure. `recording an experiment refuses a missing physical item before writing` MUST exercise recordExperiment with a valid schema and missing ItemId, assert KitLibraryItemErr (UnknownKitItemErr _) and no file/snapshot change.

**Acceptance.** After Copy experiments applies the item choices, reopening each copied experiment MUST resolve its rewritten descriptors to exactly the selected target ItemIds and parameters, distinguish same-model pieces, retain added identities, snapshots and photos, and reject missing identities before any write; mapped item files MUST remain unchanged; constructor-unit-tests, selected ui-tests, ui-smoke, build, elevation and the s22 invariants MUST pass.
